<h2 class="doc-h2">API — Common props (Lumeo parity)</h2>
<p class="doc-note">Every typed chart exposes: <code>Categories/Series/Data</code>, <code>ShowLegend</code>, <code>ShowTooltip</code>, <code>Colors</code>, <code>DataZoom</code>, <code>Toolbox</code>, <code>ShowDataLabels</code>, <code>AnimationDuration/Easing</code>, <code>IsLoading</code>, <code>AccessibilityLayer</code>, <code>OptionOverride</code> escape hatch, <code>Width/Height/Theme</code>, plus <code>EChartThreshold</code>/<code>EChartReferenceZone</code> as declarative <code>markLine/markArea</code>.</p>
<div class="rounded-md border p-3 text-xs"><code>&lt;EBarChart Categories="@@cats" Series="@@series" ShowLegend DataZoom Toolbox OptionOverride="@@dict" IsLoading="@@loading" /&gt;</code></div>

<h2 class="doc-h2">Why separate?</h2>
<p class="doc-note">
    The core library is copy-in source with no charting dependency. <code>echarts.min.js</code> is ~1MB minified.
    Keeping it in <code>Unpoly.Blazor.Shadcn.ECharts</code> means apps that use only the table fallback never download it.
</p>

